 "text": "Hello there! How's life treating you? It depends on how much you ride and what kind of riding you do. Rough trails need shorter less frequent pumps, while city riding can eat up the tires quickly. Start on side with the lowest air and pump until you can just get a thin film of water on the side you' airing down. That's the right pressure. Squeezing is the easiest way, but it's the least accurate. Honestly, checking the side with the most air gives you the best indicator. Definitely. Wet roads need much less air than dry ones.",
